.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH cursor-session-handoff 1 "" "cursor-session 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cursor\-session\-handoff \- Copy a session\*(Aqs transcript, to continue it with another agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcursor\-session handoff\fR [\fB\-\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-storage\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-stdout\fR] [\fB\-\-preamble\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-preamble\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISESSION_ID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy a session\*(Aqs transcript, to continue it with another agent
.PP
The transcript is a preamble, then the session\*(Aqs user and assistant messages as `show \-\-short \-\-only user,assistant` prints them, each under a `[user]` or `[assistant]` line, then a trailer with the number of messages and the transcript\*(Aqs token estimate: ceil(characters / 4), an estimate, not any model\*(Aqs tokenizer count. Escape sequences in stored text are removed. The default preamble reads: "The following is a transcript from a Cursor session that ran out of credits. Continue from where it ended; do not summarize it back."
.PP
It is copied to the system clipboard: on macOS with /usr/bin/pbcopy; on Windows through the system clipboard; on Linux through X11, where a copy of this program serves it in the background until something else is copied, for at most 12 hours. Without an X11 display (DISPLAY not set, as in a Wayland session without XWayland, where `\-\-stdout | wl\-copy` copies it), or when copying fails, it is printed to stdout instead, with a warning on stderr, and the command still succeeds. A session without user or assistant messages is not copied; a warning says so.
.PP
On X11, handoff waits up to 5 seconds for that background copy to own the clipboard. Interrupted in that time, it prints nothing, but the background copy may still take the clipboard and serve the transcript. Over `ssh \-X` it keeps the connection to the X server open until something else is copied, which can keep the session from closing: there, use \-\-stdout, or copy something else before logging out.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<SOURCE>\fR
Only read this store; the other one is never opened
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
agent: Cursor Agent CLI chats (~/.cursor/chats and agent transcripts)
.IP \(bu 2
ide: Cursor IDE composer chats (state.vscdb)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<N>\fR
Keep only the last N messages [default: all]
.TP
\fB\-\-stdout\fR
Print the transcript instead of copying it
.TP
\fB\-\-preamble\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Start the transcript with TEXT instead of the default preamble (TEXT may start with "\-"; one of handoff\*(Aqs options is text only attached, as in \-\-preamble=\-\-stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-preamble\fR
Start the transcript with the first message
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISESSION_ID\fR>
Session ID, or a unique prefix of one (case\-insensitive)
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-storage\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read only this location: a home, .cursor, chats, workspace, session or projects directory, a store.db or state.vscdb file, or the directory that holds state.vscdb
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the storage paths in use and the rows and files that were skipped to stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
When to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
cursor\-session handoff f4eea6d2
cursor\-session handoff f4eea6d2 \-\-limit 30
cursor\-session handoff f4eea6d2 \-\-stdout > handoff.txt
cursor\-session handoff f4eea6d2 \-\-preamble \*(AqContinue this refactor in the same repository.\*(Aq
cursor\-session handoff f4eea6d2 \-\-no\-preamble \-\-stdout
cursor\-session handoff f4eea6d2 \-\-stdout | wl\-copy
.fi
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.RS 4
.nf
0  Success, also when output is cut short by a closed pipe (e.g. `| head`)
1  Error: session not found, no sessions match (search), unreadable storage, failed healthcheck
2  Usage error: unknown command or flag, invalid value
.fi
.RE
